! conclusion: Every bell has a return path and every reply to the operator carries intent marks that can be read back.

  + IF:
    The loop's human and stakeholder edges are where learning silently dies.

  + HOWEVER:
    A bell is accepted and looks delivered, and a reply can go nowhere. Between agents this is checkable. Between agents and people it is mostly not recorded.

  + THEN:
    Every bell has a return path and every reply to the operator carries intent marks that can be read back.

  + BECAUSE:
    Learning dies silently on the human and stakeholder edges of the loop, where three of seven lifecycle stages are operator turns.

  + VALIDATION:
    Does each bell have a return path, and can each reply be read back? A holding answer covers agents only.
